  "limits": [
    "The endpoint model retains the original eight requests, rank joins, two matrix computations and 50% exposed traffic. Uniform K at eligible rows and unchanged schedule. Equal fresh Vector sparse rate and dense panel rate are reference assumptions. Effective rates use charged bytes on a shared two-way traffic calibration; they are not measured standalone Cube bandwidth.",
    "Per-query shared panel: first consumer replaces its normal ring write by publication into a generation-indexed destination and uses it immediately. The next 30 readers by layer skip their own gather and fresh panel write, and each still fetches the published panel twice. A separate full source-panel copy adds one read and one write; the sensitivity debits both. If relocation itself changes first-consumer cost, charge it. Per-layer original PV identity handoff is distinct and only priced in fold=true.",
    "Reader groups share logical KV and index source. Actual identical physical data, position/length masks, row/pair order, valid rows, PA mapping, storage lifetime, ring-slot ownership, memory availability and synchronization remain preconditions. Cross-layer retention and intra-call direct load are alternative KV budgets for the same rows. The native dictionary test still used the stock Vector gather; it cannot give the missing rates.",
    "Fractional fast rows assume the same fraction of selected-row traffic in each eligible call at equal rates and full PV fold on every nonempty compressed row. C1/C2 specializations keep the full PV handoff in both and remove panel traffic only on the named ratio. No double-counting across subsets. Null rate is not crossed by 512x in the displayed model; null row fraction is not crossed at 100%.",
    "The 64KiB Cube KV pool blocks number three. They hold at most 192 full BF16 rows in total at D512 before simultaneous work, format and event lifetime. Whole-panel single read through QK/softmax/PV is not justified for 256 or 512 rows by the current allocation. Assumed materialized-panel capacity scales with actual storage stride; a fixed 512-row ABI requires the 512 column even at lower occupancy."
  ],
